{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Trust.</b> Rabbi Moses said: the correct reading is that it means 'when you do good.'" "<b>And trust in YHWH.</b> 'Feed on faithfulness, and dwell in the land.' It is possible that the latter is the cause of the former: if you do good, you will be secure, and if you feed on faithfulness, you will dwell in the land. In my opinion: because one envies evildoers, on account of their wealth which they trust in, therefore he said: 'Trust in YHWH,' and do not refrain from doing good." "<b>And the meaning of 'dwell in the land.'</b> All the days of your life you will dwell upon the land." "<b>Feed on faithfulness.</b> Like 'guard of faithfulness,' for the one who feeds is like a guardian." "And some say: the meaning of 'and feed' is that he should not eat stolen or oppressed goods, like the sons of transgression."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:53.054999817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}